@startuml redis-04-hello-discovery
!include _style.iuml
title Why each Sentinel is told only about the master

participant "sentinel1" as S1
participant "sentinel2" as S2
participant "sentinel3" as S3
participant "**master**\n(the rendezvous)" as M
participant "replica1" as R1

note over S1, S3 #3a2c12
  Configured knowledge of each Sentinel at boot:
  **the master's ip:port and a quorum. Nothing else.**
  No Sentinel is told that the other two exist.
  No Sentinel is told that the replicas exist.
end note

S1 -> M: SUBSCRIBE __sentinel__:hello
S2 -> M: SUBSCRIBE __sentinel__:hello
S3 -> M: SUBSCRIBE __sentinel__:hello

loop every 2 seconds
  S1 -> M: PUBLISH __sentinel__:hello\n<i>ip, port, runid, epoch, my view of the master</i>
  M --> S2: (fan-out)
  M --> S3: (fan-out)
end

S2 -> M: INFO replication
M --> S2: role:master, slave0:…, slave1:…
S2 -> R1: <i>replicas discovered — never configured</i>

note over S1, R1 #12305a
  Result: a complete topology view, assembled from
  one address. Redis docs: a new Sentinel acquires the
  other Sentinels and the replica set **within 10 seconds**.
  That is what the module's 2 s stabilisation sleep is
  optimistically riding on — see FIG-03.
end note
@enduml
